<title>USA: PECO sees Pa. 1,100 MW nuke restart Thurs.</title>
<headline>PECO sees Pa. 1,100 MW nuke restart Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co's 1,100 megawatt (MW) Peach Bottom 2 nuclear power unit in Delta, Pa., shut late Tuesday after a turbine trip, is expected to restart sometime Thursday, the company said.</p>
<p>The unit automatically shut Tuesday due to an electrical problem with the turbine generator.</p>
<p>Separately, the company's 1,055 MW Limerick 2 nuclear unit in Pottstown, Pa., has returned to full power following a power reduction earlier this week, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1624</p>
</text>
